<resources>
    <!-- Fork: the themes carry NO colour of a themed surface (the black-yellow theme's rule: no
         colour is written in XML). Every colour is a settable role, applied in code from the
         role table in Roles.kt and the catalogue in Appearance.kt.

         The three items below are the one exception the rule allows: what the platform draws
         before any app code runs. The window ground, the status bar and the navigation bar of a
         starting activity are painted by the system from the theme, and a preference cannot be
         read there, so they stay literal black; each activity overwrites them from its roles in
         onCreate (Appearance.apply, SettingsActivity.onCreate). Without the window ground the
         screen flashed white coming back from the system Wi-Fi dialog (白い熊, 2026-08-10).

         The parent is the dark Material theme, not DayNight: the app is black-ground by
         default in either system mode, and a light parent would hand dark default text to any
         view the code had not reached yet. -->
    <style name="Theme.FlyingCarpet" parent="Theme.MaterialComponents.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/black</item>
    </style>
    <!-- 白い熊 魔法絨毯 UI customization page. The same rule: nothing but what the platform
         draws first. Its text fields, sliders, switches and pills are coloured in code. -->
    <style name="Theme.FlyingCarpet.Settings" parent="Theme.FlyingCarpet" />
</resources>
